hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1493","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal:\I was one of those who held up the branches from the tree away from the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was delivering the Khutbah saying: 'If it were not that dogs were a nation among nations"""""
"1494","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever acquires a dog - with the exception of a dog to guard livestock"""""
"1495","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Adi ibn Hatim, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a similar narration. Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said: This is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) hadith, and the practice (al-'amal) upon it is according to the scholars."
"1496","and Allah's Name has been mentioned over it, then eat it, provided that it was not done with a tooth or nail. And I will tell you why: As for the tooth it is a bone, and as for the nail it is the knife of the Ethiopians.' \\n"
"1497","Abū Kurayb narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from Abū Ayyūb al-Afrīqī, from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Abū al-Dardāʾ, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the eating of *al-mujaththamah*, which is the animal that is killed by being shot with arrows and then left to die.\n\nHe said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿIrbāḍ ibn Sāriyah, Anas, Ibn ʿUmar, Ibn ʿAbbās, Jābir, and Abū Hurayrah.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: The hadith of Abū al-Dardāʾ is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith."
"1498","from his father and this is more correct. 'Abayah heard from Rafi'. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1491 Arabic Hadees: 1491\"" 1499"""""
"1499","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from al-Thawri, from Simak, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that anything possessing a soul be made a target. Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. And the practice is upon it among the people of knowledge."
"1500","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid. And Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Wadak, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: \The slaughter of the unborn fetus is the slaughter of its mother.\""\n\nHe said: And in this chapter there are narrations from Jabir"
"1501","but (the narrator) did not mention in it Abayah from his father. and this is more correct. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1492 Arabic Hadees: 1492\"" 1502"""""
"1502","Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi and others narrated to us: They said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, similarly. Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. And Abu Idris al-Khawlani's name is 'A'idhullah ibn 'Abdullah."
"1503","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered two horned male sheep which were mostly white. He slaughtered them with his hand and mentioned Allah's Name"""""
"1504","**Qutaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade every animal possessing a fang from among the predatory beasts.**\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **\This is a *hasan* (good) hadith. The practice (al-'amal) according to this is held by the majority of the People of Knowledge from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be pleased with them) and others. It is also the position of 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak"
"1505","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered a horned male ram of fine pedigree"""""
"1506","Narrated Abu Kibash:\I brought a Jadha' sheep to Al-Madinah (for sale) but it remained with me. I saw Abu Hurairah and I asked him about it"""""
"1507","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey when the (Day of) Adha came"""""
"1508","Narrated Jabir:\We performed the Nahr (sacrifice) with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Al-Hudaibiyyah: A camel for seven (persons) and a cow for seven (persons)"""""
"1509","Narrated Hujayyah bin 'Adi:\Ali said: 'A cow is for seven.' I said: \""And if it gives birth?' He said: 'Then slaughter its offspring with it.' I said: 'What if it is lame?' He said: 'When it has reached the place of ritual.' I said: 'What if it has a broken horn?' He said: 'There is no harm"""""
"1510","Narrated 'Ali:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that an animal with a A'dab (stump) horn or ear should be slaughtered as a sacrifice.\"" Qatadah (one of the narrators) said: \""So I mentioned this to Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab and he said: 'The A'dab is that which equals or more than that"""""
"1511","Narrated 'Ata bin Yasar:\I asked Abu Abyub [Al-Ansari] how the slaughtering was done during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'A man would sacrifice a sheep for himself and the people in his household. They would eat from it and feed others"""""
"1512","Narrated Jabalah bin Suhaim :That a man asked Ibn 'Umar about the Udhiyah"
"1513","Narrated Ibn 'Umar :\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed in Al-Madinah for ten years performing the Udhiyah"""""
"1514","Narrated Al-Bara' bin 'Azib :\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us on the Day of Nahr and he said: 'None of you should slaughter until he performs the Salat.\"" He said: 'So my maternal uncle stood and said: ' O Messenger of Allah"""""
"1515","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days"""""
"1516","Narrated Sulaiman bin Buraidah:From his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I used to prohibit you from (eating) the meat of Sacrifice beyond three days so that those who have the ability would give to those who do not have it. So (now) eat as you like"""""
"1517","Narrated 'Abis bin Rabi'ah:\I said to the Mother of the Believers: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibit from the meat of the sacrifice?' She said: 'No"""""
"1518","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no Fara' or 'Atirah.\"" The Fara' is the first of the offspring that would be born to them"""""
"1519","Narrated Yusuf bin Mahak:They entered upon Hafsah bint 'Abdur-Rahman to ask her about the 'Aqiqah. She informed them that 'Aishah had informed her"
"1520","Narrated 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi':That his father said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say the Adhan in the ear of Al-Hasan bin 'Ali - when he was born to Fatimah - the Adhan of Salat"""""
"1521","Narrated Umm Kurz:That she asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the 'Aqiqah. He said: \For the boy is two sheep"""""
"1522","Narrated Mikhnaf bin Sulaim:\We were standing with the Prophet (ﷺ) at 'Arafat when I heard him say: 'O you people! For every household each year is Udhiyah (sacrifice) and 'Atirah. Do you know what an 'Atirah is ? It is that which you call Ar-Rajabiyyah"""""
"1523","Narrated Muhammad bin 'Ali bin Al-Husain:That Ali bin Abi Talib said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had the 'Aqiqah for Al-Hasan with one sheep"""""
